%% Switch the backend policy of an agent from organization to personal (I1, I3, I4).
%% Domain details and guided flow: 10-backend-policy.md.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant O as Owner (console)
  box api node
    participant AG as agents
    participant AZ as authz
    participant HUB as gateway hub
  end
  participant DB as PostgreSQL
  participant AD as Agent adapter
  participant B as Whoever runs the runtime
  participant APP as Apps of the readers

  O->>AG: step-up with passkey or device key
  O->>AG: POST agents/{id}/billing-mode (personal, credential_holder_id, reason)
  AG->>AZ: authorize(Owner, agent.billing_mode.set, agent): Owner and step-up
  AG->>DB: BEGIN, lock permission_version first
  AG->>DB: UPDATE agents billing_mode, credential_holder_id, billing_mode_changed_at and _by
  AG->>AZ: before the commit: I1 check
  AZ->>AZ: compute the set with effective level trigger on all targets of the agent
  alt set is not exactly the credential_holder
    AZ-->>AG: invariant_violation, code i1_violation
    AG->>DB: ROLLBACK
    AG->>DB: own transaction: audit entry decision deny
    AG-->>O: 409 with hint "switch to organization first" or adjust grants
  else I1 holds
    AG->>DB: events agent.updated, access.changed for those affected, audit allow, COMMIT
    AG-->>O: 200
    HUB-->>APP: agent.updated: badge Personal
    HUB-->>AD: agent.updated with new configured mode (received via agent.read as agent-self)
  end
  AD->>AG: heartbeat: reported_billing_mode organization
  AG->>AG: configured and reported mode differ: state degraded, warning in console and agent card
  Note over AD: Every token now carries billing_mode personal. The adapter starts nothing while its reported mode differs, and reports billing_mode_mismatch (I3)
  B->>AD: switch the runtime outside the product (profile environment, restart)
  AD->>AG: heartbeat: reported_billing_mode personal
  AG->>AG: configured equals reported mode, warning goes away
  Note over O,APP: Switching all agents (agent.billing_mode.set_all) works the same way, in one transaction
